    "title": "Aaliyah Diggs records 1,000th dig in Little Giants' win over Bison | High School | dnronline.com",
    "text": "Waynesboro won its second straight with a thrilling 25-19, 25-21, 18-25, 22-25, 16-14 victory over Shenandoah District opponent Buffalo Gap in Swoope on Tuesday.\nSenior standout Aaliyah Diggs enjoyed a special night for the Little Giants, finishing with 26 digs and surpassing 1,000 for her career.\nMorgan Sites totaled 16 kills, 16 assists and 23 digs for Waynesboro, while Morgan Harlow had 21 assists and 12 digs.\nSenior outside hitter Jordan Smith added seven kills for the Giants, while Dylan Coffey had 12 digs and five aces, and Ella Cox racked up four blocks.\nFor the Bison, who have dropped 11 straight, Bailey Tribble continued to impress with 27 kills, 22 digs and three aces.\nGap sophomore setter Avery Wheeler had 36 assists, 22 digs and four aces, while Brailyn Green finished with 15 digs and a pair of aces, and Violet Patterson added 10 kills and five digs of her own.\nWaynesboro (10-10, 8-6 Shenandoah) returns to action on Thursday at district foe Riverheads, while the Bison (3-14, 1-12 Shenandoah) travel to Alleghany for a league match on Thursday.",
